    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe rename/consolidation itself is clean and well-documented \u2014 `CheckHouseholdUnique`/`HouseholdDuplicateException`/`HouseholdDuplicateExceptionHandler` follow the existing naming conventions, `OwnerIdentity` and the stale `OwnerTelephone`/`Owner` doc references were removed consistently, and `Household` is correctly left as the single source of truth. The problem is one unit:\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate` has become a vestigial no-op, but keeps the shape of a real algorithm.**\n\nTrace the new `service` body: it loops over all owners, and the only action inside the loop is `return` when a same-last-name-and-postcode owner is found. There is no longer any code path that sets `possibleDuplicate = true` or `possibleDuplicateOf`. So the method provably always leaves the owner unflagged \u2014 the entire loop, `isSelf`, and `equalsIgnoreCase` exist only to compute a value that is never used to change state.\n\nThis is dead structure that actively misleads a maintainer:\n- A class named `FlagPossibleDuplicate` that can never flag anything reads as a bug or an unfinished edit, not as intended behaviour. The javadoc explains *why* it's always false, but the 20 lines of iteration underneath contradict that intent at a glance.\n- If the step must stay in both pipelines, its body should collapse to what it actually does (unconditionally ensure the flag is false), dropping the loop and now-unused helpers \u2014 or the team should decide whether the step/field is still warranted at all. Retaining a full scan whose only outcome is `return` is the kind of logic-in-the-wrong-shape that should be resolved as part of this change, not left behind it.\n\nRelatedly, note for the maintainer: because this method can no longer set them, `Owner.possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (and the `getPossibleDuplicateOf` accessor referenced in the javadoc) are now permanently `false`/`null`. That's arguably a spec consequence rather than a structural defect, but it reinforces that `FlagPossibleDuplicate` and its loop should be reduced to their real behaviour rather than preserved as-is.",
